+- The chat lane calls `memory.skipReview`, the same skip J17 "don't remember this" uses. It also runs for a refused or
+  not-yet-built setting: those words are still an instruction to foo.
 
 ## (d) Review
 
-Pending.
+Fable, high tier, 2026-10-22: **PASS WITH FIXES**. It ran the tests on main's `src` (both fail) and here (both pass).
+
+- Act on, fixed: the skip landed after the intake turn. A review already waiting for 20 s of quiet (after an earlier
+  reply) only restarted its timer on the new message, so a slow intake turn (Claude CLI turns take 20 s or more) let it
+  fire mid-turn and read "Switch to dark mode" first. A new user message now cancels the pending review (§12.4 Trigger),
+  with a test for that case.
+- Considers: a mixed message ("switch to dark mode, my eyes hurt at night") loses its second fact. This is intentional:
+  the spec sentence leaves out the whole message by intake kind, and the user can still say it again or add it on the
+  Memory page. The `unsaved` set grows per session only, as it already does for J17.
